Types Casting - Converting a type (int, String or custom class) from one type to another

Types of conversion - Implicit conversion - No data loss
					- Explicit conversion - Data loss may happen
					- User - defined conversion - DOne via user code with helper classes
var or implicitly-typed variable - Local variable is strongly typed just as if you had declared the type yourself, but the compiler determines the type

working with mothos - Method is a code block that contains a series of statements. A program causes the statements to be execute by calling the method and specifying any required 
